From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phonepanel <phonepanel@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:54:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] extract-cert: build without OpenSSL's ENGINE API

OpenSSL 4 (and 3.x built with no-engine) defines OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE and has no ENGINE_* functions, so
linking scripts/extract-cert failed. Skip the PKCS#11 branch as for BoringSSL; sign-file.c in this tree
already does the same. PhoneKit's builds never extract certificates from PKCS#11.
---
 scripts/extract-cert.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/extract-cert.c b/scripts/extract-cert.c
index 68f73787d..e093bf41b 100644
--- a/scripts/extract-cert.c
+++ b/scripts/extract-cert.c
@@ -21,7 +21,9 @@
 #include <openssl/bio.h>
 #include <openssl/pem.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
+#ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
+#endif
 
 /*
  * OpenSSL 3.0 deprecates the OpenSSL's ENGINE API.
@@ -121,8 +123,8 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 		fclose(f);
 		exit(0);
 	} else if (!strncmp(cert_src, "pkcs11:", 7)) {
-#ifdef OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL
-		ERR(1, "BoringSSL does not support extracting from PKCS#11");
+#if defined(OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL) || defined(OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE)
+		ERR(1, "this OpenSSL does not support extracting from PKCS#11 (no ENGINE)");
 		exit(1);
 #else
 		ENGINE *e;
-- 
2.56.1

